        <onset>2025-08-06T19:13:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-06T20:00:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Morristown TN</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 6 at 7:13PM EDT by NWS Morristown TN</headline>
        <description>At 712 PM EDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Huntsville, or near Oneida, moving southeast at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Jacksboro, Huntsville, Caryville, Cove Lake State Park, Smokey
Junction, Royal Blue, and Norma.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Frequent cloud to ground lightning is occurring with this storm.
Lightning can strike 10 miles away from a thunderstorm. Seek a safe
shelter inside a building or vehicle.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SPSMRX</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WWUS84 KMRX 062313</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A STRONG THUNDERSTORM WILL IMPACT WEST CENTRAL CAMPBELL AND SOUTHEASTERN SCOTT COUNTIES THROUGH 800 PM EDT</value>
