        <expires>2025-08-07T20:15:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Wilmington OH</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 7 at 7:40PM EDT by NWS Wilmington OH</headline>
        <description>At 739 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located over Independence,
moving south at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and very heavy rain.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Visibility will be poor and hydroplaning
is possible.

Locations impacted include...
Florence, Independence, Erlanger, Edgewood, Elsmere, Highland
Heights, Taylor Mill, Walton, Claryville, Union, Crittenden, Wilder,
Cold Spring, Ryland Heights, Fairview, Visalia, Atwood, Richwood,
and Grants Lick.

This includes the following Interstates...
I-71 in Kentucky between mile markers 76 and 77.
I-75 in Kentucky between mile markers 167 and 180.

If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a sturdy building.

Motorists should slow down and use extra caution.

To report hazardous weather conditions, go to our website at
weather.gov/iln and submit your report via social media, when you can
do so safely.
</description>
