        <senderName>NWS North Platte NE</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 7 at 6:55PM CDT by NWS North Platte NE</headline>
        <description>At 655 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 8
miles south of Nenzel, or 28 miles west of Valentine, moving east at
15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Anderson Bridge State Wildlife Management Area.

This includes the following highways...
Highway 20 between mile markers 178 and 181.
Highway 97 between mile markers 124 and 125.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
