        <senderName>NWS New Orleans LA</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 7 at 7:23PM CDT by NWS New Orleans LA</headline>
        <description>At 723 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Port Allen, moving southwest at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Winds in excess of 40 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Baton Rouge, Port Allen, Brusly, Maringouin, Rosedale, Grosse Tete,
Ramah, and Erwinville.

This includes the following Interstates...
Interstate 10 in Louisiana between mile markers 134 and 154.
Interstate 110 in Louisiana between mile markers 1 and 4.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
