        <senderName>NWS Cheyenne WY</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 8 at 4:49PM MDT by NWS Cheyenne WY</headline>
        <description>At 449 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking gusty showers along a line
extending from near Rawhide Buttes to near Laramie Peak. Movement was
southeast at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Wheatland, Guernsey, Fort Laramie, Hartville, Chugcreek, Lakeview
North, Westview Circle, Y-O Ranch, Register Cliff State Historic
Site, Friend Park Campground, Sandy Cove Campground, Laramie Peak,
Guernsey State Park, Pine Ridge Estates, Phifer Airfield, Jay Em,
Oregon Trail Ruts State Historic Site, Dwyer Junction, Fort Laramie
National Historic Site, and Grayrocks Reservoir.

This includes Interstate 25 in Wyoming between mile markers 77 and
105.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
