        <expires>2025-08-08T18:00:00-06:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Cheyenne WY</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 8 at 5:03PM MDT by NWS Cheyenne WY</headline>
        <description>At 502 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking gusty showers along a line
extending from 11 miles west of Bow River Campground to 6 miles
northwest of Wheatland Reservoir Number 3. Movement was southeast at
15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Albany, Medicine Bow, Rock River, Elk Mountain, Bosler, Brooklyn Lake
Campground, McFadden, Nash Fork Campground, Wheatland Reservoir
Number 3, Rob Roy Reservoir, Arlington, Turpin Reservoir, Brooklyn
Lake, Sugar Loaf Campground, Libby Creek Campground, Bow River
Campground, Deep Creek Campground, Sybille Canyon, Centennial, and
Snowy Range Pass.

This includes Interstate 80 in Wyoming between mile markers 253 and
300.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
