        <severity>Moderate</severity>
        <certainty>Observed</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-08T19:11:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-08T19:11:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-08T20:00:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Marquette MI</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 8 at 7:11PM EDT by NWS Marquette MI</headline>
        <description>At 710 PM EDT/610 PM CDT/, Doppler radar was tracking a strong
thunderstorm near Hurley, or 7 miles northwest of Ironwood, moving
east at 25 mph.

HAZARD...Winds in excess of 30 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Ironwood, Bessemer, Wakefield, Hurley, Thomaston, Little Girls Point,
Clark Lake, Ironwood Airport, and Copper Peak.

People attending Blasting at Copper Peak should seek safe shelter
immediately!
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SPSMQT</value>
        </parameter>
