FXUS63 KIWX 082325

AFDIWX



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Northern Indiana

725 PM EDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Hot and humid through Monday with highs in the upper 80s to 

  near 90 and heat indices in the low to mid 90s. 



- Chances for showers and storms returns next week, with low 

  confidence on exact timing and locations to be impacted.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 139 PM EDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Torrid upper ridge will amplify a bit further near term before 

flattening across the Great Lakes somewhat late weekend. This 

in turn should allow for composite outflow/cold frontal zone to 

sink sewd into at least northwest portions of the area later Sunday

night, providing chances for tstorms that will then extend 

through mid week timed with active storm track through srn 

Canada. Hottest temps expected Sat - Mon beneath heart of upper 

ridge yet temps expected to continue well above normal through 

the week with reamplification of upper ridge likely again by 

next weekend. In between, proximity of stalled frontal zone 

implied across parts of the area supports chance pops tied to 

the diurnal curve, mainly afternoon and evening.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z SUNDAY/...

Issued at 720 PM EDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Diurnally driven VFR cu will quickly dissipate shortly after 

the start of the period, only to develop once again mid to late 

morning Saturday. Winds will follow a similar trend to the

clouds, becoming light and eventually climbing back to 10 kts or

so as mixing increases during Saturday. 



&&



.IWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

IN...None.

OH...None.

MI...None.

MARINE...None.



&&



$$



DISCUSSION...T

AVIATION...Fisher



