        <senderName>NWS Chicago IL</senderName>
        <headline>Marine Weather Statement issued August 9 at 7:53PM CDT by NWS Chicago IL</headline>
        <description>The areas affected include...

Nearshore Waters from Winthrop Harbor to Wilmette Harbor...
Open Waters from Winthrop Harbor to Wilmette Harbor out to Mid
Lake...

At 752 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated a couple of strong
thunderstorms, capable of producing winds around 30 knots. These
storms were located over Waukegan Harbor, and south to near
Lake Bluff, both moving northeast at 20 knots.

Locations impacted include...
Winthrop Harbor and Waukegan Harbor.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners can expect gusty winds to around 30 knots, locally higher
waves, and lightning strikes. Boaters should seek safe harbor
immediately until this storm passes.</instruction>
